#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:10
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:12
msgid ""
"Define the shape of the `## Kickoff` section in `spec.md` — a terse, "
"model-optimized cold-start prompt the user pastes into a fresh session "
"when they want to pick this spec back up after a context break."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:16
msgid "A kickoff prompt is **not** a documentation summary. It's a *prompt*:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:17
msgid "60–120 tokens (hard cap 200)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:18
msgid ""
"Tells a fresh model what this spec is, where it stands, where to pick up,"
" and which 2–5 files to open first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:20
msgid ""
"Aggressive on signal-to-noise. The spec body has the documentation; the "
"kickoff has only what gets you productive in 30 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:23
msgid ""
"The kickoff is **part of the spec**, not a projection. Skills (`/design`,"
" `/deliver`, `/diagnose`) write it inline as they author or mutate the "
"spec. There is no auto-refresh hook. If a kickoff goes stale, the fix is "
"to re-run the workflow or hand-edit — same as any other spec content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:28
msgid "When to write or update me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:30
msgid ""
"**`/design`** — write a fresh `## Kickoff` as part of scaffolding the new"
" spec, between `## Goal` and `## Problem`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:32
msgid ""
"**`/deliver`** — rewrite `## Kickoff` when the spec's status flips "
"(planning → delivering, delivering → completed) or when a meaningful "
"chunk lands. The \"Pick up at:\" line should always reflect *now*, not "
"\"two commits ago.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:36
msgid ""
"**`/diagnose`** — same pattern when bug specs flip from `triaging` → "
"`delivering`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:38
msgid ""
"**Hand-edit** — anytime the user changes direction or wants to tune the "
"opener. The spec is source of truth; edit it like any other section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:42
msgid ""
"A kickoff that says *\"pick up at X\"* when X already shipped is "
"misleading. A kickoff that's still accurate doesn't need refreshing for "
"refresh's sake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:45
msgid "Format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:47
msgid ""
"## Kickoff\n"
"\n"
"<1 line: what this spec is, in the user's vocabulary. Avoid jargon\n"
"the user wouldn't say themselves.>\n"
"\n"
"**Status:** <planning|delivering|blocked|in-review> — <last meaningful\n"
"turn, 1 line>\n"
"\n"
"**Pick up at:** <concrete next step, 1–2 lines. Specific enough that\n"
"a fresh model can act without re-reading the whole spec.>\n"
"\n"
"→ <runnable pointer: spec path, slash command, or shell command>\n"
"\n"
"**Files:** <2–5 path:line refs the model will need to open first>\n"
"**Skip:** <1 line of approaches already rejected — only if non-empty>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:65
msgid ""
"Sections after `Files:` are omitted entirely when empty. Don't write "
"`Skip: (none)`; just leave the line out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:68
msgid "Section guidance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:70
msgid ""
"**First line (the what)** — phrase as the user would say it aloud, not as"
" the spec title. Example: *\"Adds `## Kickoff` sections to every spec and"
" a `hero queue` command for the ranked backlog.\"* — the spec title is "
"more formal; the kickoff line is the elevator-blurb."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:74
msgid ""
"**Status** — one of `planning`, `delivering`, `blocked`, `in-review`. "
"Append a half-sentence on the *last meaningful turn* — what just happened"
" that a fresh session needs to know. Don't describe everything done so "
"far; the spec body has that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:78
msgid ""
"**Pick up at** — the *one specific thing* a fresh session should attempt."
" Don't list options. If there are forks, pick the highest-leverage next "
"step and name only that. The user can re-tune the kickoff if they pivot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:82
msgid ""
"**→ pointer** — must be runnable as-is. A spec path "
"(`.hero/specs/foo/spec.md`), a slash command (`/deliver foo`), or a shell"
" command. Not a sentence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:84
msgid ""
"**Files** — 2–5 file paths with optional `:line` markers. These are the "
"files the fresh session will need to open first. Pick load-bearing ones, "
"not every file in `## Changes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:87
msgid ""
"**Skip** — gold when present. One line per approach already rejected, so "
"the next session doesn't re-suggest it. Omit the heading entirely when "
"there's nothing to skip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:91
msgid "Quality bar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:93
msgid ""
"A good kickoff is one a fresh session can paste and immediately be "
"productive — no follow-up \"what's the spec?\" or \"where are the "
"files?\" questions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:97
msgid "The new session should know after reading it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:98
msgid "**What this spec is** — first line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:99
msgid "**Where it stands now** — Status line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:100
msgid "**What to attempt next** — Pick up at + → pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:101
msgid "**Which files matter** — Files line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:102
msgid "**What not to try** — Skip line, when present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:104
msgid ""
"If you can't picture a fresh session being productive after pasting the "
"kickoff, add detail. If it's becoming a transcript of everything done, "
"cut detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:108
msgid ""
"**Hard cap on kickoff body: 200 tokens. Target: 60–120.** If it's running"
" over, the spec body is doing the kickoff's job — point at the spec body "
"and trim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:112
msgid "Worked examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:114
msgid "Good — small spec, mid-delivery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:116
msgid ""
"## Kickoff\n"
"\n"
"<!-- drift-test:ignore (illustrative: this kickoff documents a phantom-"
"command bug — `hero nudge` is intentionally stale) -->\n"
"Renames stale docs from `hero nudge` to `hero relevant` so file-aware\n"
"context examples match the current CLI.\n"
"\n"
"**Status:** delivering — CLI examples are fixed; MCP docs still need a\n"
"note that the tool remains named `hero_nudge`.\n"
"\n"
"<!-- drift-test:ignore (illustrative: same kickoff example as above) -->\n"
"**Pick up at:** sweep docs for `hero nudge` and replace user-facing CLI\n"
"examples with `hero relevant`, while leaving MCP tool names intact.\n"
"\n"
"→ `rg \"hero nudge|hero_nudge\" docs README.md GETTING-STARTED.md`\n"
"\n"
"**Files:** README.md, GETTING-STARTED.md, docs/cli/search-and-context.md\n"
"**Skip:** renaming `hero_nudge` in MCP docs — that tool name is still "
"real.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:136
msgid "Good — large spec, planning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:138
msgid ""
"## Kickoff\n"
"\n"
"Adds `## Kickoff` sections to every spec and a root-level `hero queue`\n"
"command so the user can see all ready-to-work specs at a glance and\n"
"copy-paste a session opener for any of them.\n"
"\n"
"**Status:** planning — spec just landed, no code yet.\n"
"\n"
"**Pick up at:** start with the parser change — add `Pinned bool` to\n"
"`internal/spec/spec.go` and a `Kickoff()` accessor reading from\n"
"`Sections[\"kickoff\"]`. Tests next. Bigger work (selector + commands)\n"
"is Phase 2.\n"
"\n"
"→ `.hero/specs/kickoff-prompts-queue/spec.md`\n"
"\n"
"**Files:** `internal/spec/spec.go`, `internal/spec/spec_test.go`, `skills"
"/kickoff-prompt.md`\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:157
msgid "Anti-pattern — bloated, vague"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:159
msgid ""
"## Kickoff\n"
"\n"
"This spec is about improving developer experience around session\n"
"continuity by introducing a structured way to capture the essential\n"
"context needed to resume work after a break. It involves several\n"
"components including format definitions, command surfaces, integration\n"
"with existing workflows, and tooling support. We have considered\n"
"several approaches and settled on a hybrid model that balances\n"
"flexibility with consistency.\n"
"\n"
"**Status:** in progress\n"
"\n"
"**Pick up at:** various tasks remain. See spec body for full list.\n"
"\n"
"**Files:** see Changes section\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:177
msgid ""
"What's wrong: prose where pointers should be, no concrete next step, no "
"file paths, no actionable pointer, lists nothing the user can paste and "
"act on. The spec body should be doing this work; the kickoff has failed "
"if it just defers to the body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:182
msgid "Composing with related skills"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:184
msgid ""
"**`next-md`** — governs the `.hero/NEXT.md` agent half (this turn's "
"status). Different surface: NEXT.md is the *current session* handoff; the"
" kickoff is the *cold-start* prompt for any spec in the queue. Both can "
"co-exist; both have their own format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:188
msgid ""
"**`end-of-turn-recap`** — governs the closing message of the current "
"turn. When the recap rule's spin-off offer points at a spec, it "
"references the spec's kickoff (`hero_kickoff <slug>`) rather than "
"reproducing prompt content inline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:192
msgid ""
"**`hero queue` / `hero list --format kickoff`** — the surfacing layer. "
"The selector picks ready specs and renders their `## Kickoff` bodies. The"
" kickoff format is what makes the queue useful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:196
msgid "What not to do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:198
msgid "Don't reproduce the spec body. Reference, don't repeat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:199
msgid ""
"Don't list every file in `## Changes`. Pick the 2–5 the fresh session "
"needs first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:201
msgid "Don't write a paragraph where one line works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:202
msgid "Don't leave stale kickoffs around. If `Pick up at:` is wrong, fix it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:203
msgid ""
"Don't put commit hashes, branch names, or session-specific runtime state "
"in the kickoff. That belongs in NEXT.md, not the spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/kickoff-prompt/SKILL.md:205
msgid "Don't forget the `→ pointer` line — runnable, not prose."
msgstr ""

